 "pin_regs": {
  "enable": false,
  "reason": "Pin stages are RTL, not flow: the strap inputs pc__pc / pc__cfg_stack (the 6-11 level input cones of SAFE-AUDIT-KV) land in KEPT pin registers (qkd_static_kv_pc_path_fan_nc_b pc_sr/st_sr + chain station spc/sst, 0 schedule cycles: constant die straps); every chain / boot / HBM word (i_next/i_prev/i_grp/i_grp_h/pc__pi/pc__hes/pc__land_er) is flop-direct (depth 0, kvs_port_domains).  A flow-inserted stage on those would add a cycle to every priced static-join edge age (die_ages.json / kv_static_ages) that the compiled calendar does not have.  Waived (depth <= 3 or fault-only): pc__ki (hck kick word, depth 3: a stage would move the priced kick age), x__est__0_1 (emb boot-ready level, depth 1), pc__fi (fault-chain sticky OR, 1 sink, fault-only; 0.8 T hck budget)."
 },
